  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan: Strengthening Service Delivery for Migrants (SSDM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen access to justice for returnees through the delivery of comprehensive legal services and structured case management, ensuring that vulnerable populations are able to resolve legal challenges and secure their rights. 2) To promote inclusive dialogue and legal awareness in order to foster mutual understanding and reduce tensions between returnees and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Female lawyers, IOM staff, IOM partners involved in legal information and support, community members in selected areas of high return.Indirect beneficiaries: Host communities and returnees, including female-headed households in the selected areas of high return.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support a sustainable and dignified return of Afghans and to strengthen social cohesion with host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
